From: syabyr <syabyr@github.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 12:10:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] phy: rockchip: inno-usb2: skip OTG sm for peripheral mode

The OTG state machine and BC1.2 charger detection run for every port
whose controller dr_mode is neither "host" nor unknown, including
peripheral-only ports.  A peripheral port is owned by a USB gadget
controller (e.g. dwc3 in gadget mode) that keeps the PHY powered while
its gadget driver is bound.

On such ports the OTG machinery is harmful: when utmi_bvalid reads 0
(or flaps) while the gadget is enumerated, the charger detect work
toggles the controller into non-driving mode and powers the PHY off,
and the OTG state machine's UNDEFINED/DCP paths power the PHY off too -
killing the active gadget connection a few seconds after enumeration.
On the EmbedFire LubanCat 1N (RK3566, RNDIS gadget on usb_host0_xhci),
the host sees the RNDIS device disconnect exactly 2s after boot and 6s
after every dwc3 rebind, with clk_usbphy0_480m disabled and dwc3 ep0
enable failing afterwards.

Treat USB_DR_MODE_PERIPHERAL like HOST/UNKNOWN in
rockchip_usb2phy_otg_port_init() (skip the OTG state machine, charger
detection and extcon notifier registration), in
rockchip_usb2phy_init() (do not enable bvalid/id IRQs nor schedule
otg_sm_work) and in rockchip_usb2phy_exit() (symmetric cancellation).

The PHY power state of a peripheral port then stays fully owned by the
gadget controller through the standard phy power_on/power_off ops.

Signed-off-by: syabyr <syabyr@github.com>
---
 drivers/phy/rockchip/phy-rockchip-inno-usb2.c | 15 ++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/phy/rockchip/phy-rockchip-inno-usb2.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/rockchip/phy-rockchip-inno-usb2.c
@@ -511,6 +511,7 @@
 
 	if (rport->port_id == USB2PHY_PORT_OTG) {
 		if (rport->mode != USB_DR_MODE_HOST &&
+		    rport->mode != USB_DR_MODE_PERIPHERAL &&
 		    rport->mode != USB_DR_MODE_UNKNOWN) {
 			/* clear bvalid status and enable bvalid detect irq */
 			ret = property_enable(rphy->grf,
@@ -652,6 +653,7 @@
 
 	if (rport->port_id == USB2PHY_PORT_OTG &&
 	    rport->mode != USB_DR_MODE_HOST &&
+	    rport->mode != USB_DR_MODE_PERIPHERAL &&
 	    rport->mode != USB_DR_MODE_UNKNOWN) {
 		cancel_delayed_work_sync(&rport->otg_sm_work);
 		cancel_delayed_work_sync(&rport->chg_work);
@@ -1308,7 +1310,16 @@
 	mutex_init(&rport->mutex);
 
 	rport->mode = of_usb_get_dr_mode_by_phy(child_np, -1);
+	/*
+	 * A peripheral-only port has no OTG role switching to manage.
+	 * Skip the OTG state machine and BC1.2 charger detection: their
+	 * opmode toggling and power_off() calls kill an active gadget
+	 * connection (e.g. RNDIS) a few seconds after enumeration on
+	 * boards whose utmi_bvalid reads erratically while the gadget
+	 * is running.
+	 */
 	if (rport->mode == USB_DR_MODE_HOST ||
+	    rport->mode == USB_DR_MODE_PERIPHERAL ||
 	    rport->mode == USB_DR_MODE_UNKNOWN) {
 		ret = 0;
 		goto out;
